  "equivalence_and_ownership": [
    "c354.private_state begins with a fresh built-in tree copy and validates original schema, epoch, height, root generations, exact t/m support, all named full keys/preimages, duplicates/collisions/capacity, fixed boundary and selected union. On its own returned state under the same pinned authority, the same ordered data reconstruct equal t/m maps, selected/excluded sets and original names. This is a raw Source proof of value idempotence, not a replay or digest-only acceptance.",
    "The new _checked_state_projection executes the full former private_state body. Its return is (old_marked_six_tuple, original_projection_six_tuple). The public private_state wrapper returns only the first element and remains fresh on every invocation. No checked context is supplied by a caller.",
    "The original tuple is already complete before the independent marked check. The independent9fd function clones its full packet, separately invokes c354/private original and membership checks, rebuilds every decorated selected packet, compares the full extra-channel union and rechecks full original authority. None of those calls is removed or replaced by the reused tuple.",
    "Within _filter, original t/m/selected/excluded are read-only inputs to c354.legality. with_obligations mutates only each newly cloned candidate tile, not the totals. The returned marked t map aliases that checked original totals map, which is safe because neither path writes it. The original names ledger remains separate because marked private-state construction copies it with dict(base_names) before candidate and decorated collision updates.",
    "All tuple references are synchronous function locals. They are not stored on self, delegated as authority, placed in receipts/checkpoints/cursors, or reused across calls, proposer/checker endpoints, revisions, rollbacks or engine decisions. base_state and every other public/private nonfilter path remain fresh/raw exact.",
    "All remaining native tick/callback/Source-boundary/resource exceptions still propagate. Removed duplicate traversals imply different charged work and possible finite-budget outcomes; no exact callback-count/exception-time equivalence is claimed. No counter is reset and no ResourceError/UNKNOWN is coerced. The scope is trusted synchronous pinned Sources and ticks, not hostile mutating/reentrant callbacks."
  ],
